"open":{"price":"Three lines carry parts their pages do not show: the ADREC paragraph (the 27 Feb 2026 release date is not on the Zawya page, Yas Island's ~15% share cannot be read off the ADREC H1 2025 chart, and the dashboard 'no static export' remark has no listed source); the Saadiyat luxury-villa row's sub-community list (HIDD Al Saadiyat, Mamsha, beachfront) and the Al Reem row's 'overwhelmingly apartment stock' gloss are not on the Bayut FY 2025 page. Their figures (AED 25 bn, ~82%, ~33%, +19% / +13%, AED 2,061 / +12.9%, AED 1,352 / +18.9%) do match. Every other line is confirmed or labelled.","tax":"Not closable yet: (1) the DM Housing Fee line's listed pages don't support DEWA collection or '12 instalments' (the DEWA page wasn't readable; u.ae only says monthly electricity and water bills; the DEWA consumer FAQ says DEWA collects the housing fee on behalf of DM and should be cited instead); (2) the DLD transfer line's 'market practice = buyer pays full 4%' has no source; (3) the 'UAE nationals exempt from housing fee on owner-occupied property' row has no authority at all. Items 2 and 3 also need the corrections above.","risks":"The Post-2020 build-era row (confirmed line 3) is not fully supported: 'Al Sa'fat – Dubai Green Building System' is on none of its pages, and the WAM capture says only 'on Friday, during Expo 2020 Dubai's Water Week' with no Mar 2022 date. The section note's claim that the federal codes (WAM, Mar 2022) were confirmed therefore does not hold. The 'Implication for buyers' line (Mirdif, Al Quoz, Sharjah border areas, IMPZ water-logging) also has no source."}}
